{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Gauss.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"image\"><img alt=\"image\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/eb/Gauss.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"170\" height=\"148\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The diagram shown consists of circles with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66affac74027bd2b791cd2d31fa60abf7a373312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\,\\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and semi-circles with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66affac74027bd2b791cd2d31fa60abf7a373312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\,\\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. The total shaded area, in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb06de78ae4ef6fc2731e0abb6788477c03a7b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cm}^2$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f62174a0f612f6de43c058ad6120d0539d8ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~10\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~9.5\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~9\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~8.5\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~8\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> full circles each with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> half circles each with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8efc60a1547dcb02df3995b9b35771fdee9f9c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"38\" />, so the total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312b682d0325bd4b34951fe8139c3de38ea8c18d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\pi+4\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\pi=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;r